-- short.win indexer — the API contract tests' seed (INDEXER.md §11.2). Owner: API.
--
-- A small, internally consistent indexed history (as the writer and the projections would leave
-- it) used by tests/api_*.rs until replayed sessions exist (§13.5 join 2). Three markets:
--   A  raydium_v4, tier B: three lenders (one the coin creator), positions open / closed /
--      CR-liquidated / S1 / S3, a fast-path pool window, a coverage gap and pause, fees swept;
--   B  pump_swap, tier C: one lender across a rebase epoch, positions expired / S2 /
--      liquidated-at-expiry / open;
--   J  a junk listing (no lenders, no positions; an over-long name).
-- Plus governance (applied, pending, cancelled, superseded changes), the global pause, a
-- disabled venue, a broken route, venue extras, the venue-upgrade latch, venue trades for
-- candles, hourly rollups, an oracle price and API keys. Slots 1000-1047, one block every
-- 600 s from 1790000000; finalized up to slot 1030.
